
# Node.js — From Browser JavaScript to Server JavaScript


> **“Where does JavaScript run?”**

Students will probably say:

> Browser.

> “Can JavaScript run without Chrome?”

Don't answer immediately.

Write:

```js
console.log("Hello");
```

> “Who provides `console`?”

This is the first important mental model.

---

# 1. JavaScript is a language, not a browser

Tell them:

JavaScript itself doesn't know about:

```js
document
window
localStorage
fetch
alert
```

Those are **APIs provided by an environment**.

This distinction is extremely important.

### Browser

```text
JavaScript
   +
JavaScript Engine
   +
Browser APIs
   ↓
Browser Environment
```

Examples:

```js
document
window
localStorage
fetch
setTimeout
```

### Node.js

```text
JavaScript
   +
V8 JavaScript Engine
   +
Node.js APIs
   ↓
Node.js Environment
```

Examples:

```js
process
fs
path
http
os
crypto
```

