# 16. Strict mode

Now this becomes natural.

Ask:

> “What happens if JavaScript code accidentally creates a global variable?”

```js
name = "Abhishek";
```

In sloppy mode this can behave unexpectedly.

Try:

```js
"use strict";

name = "Abhishek";
```

You'll get an error similar to:

```text
ReferenceError: name is not defined
```

Explain:

```js
"use strict";
```

enables strict mode.

But here's the important modern point:

> **ES modules are automatically strict mode.**

So:

```js
<script type="module">
```

and Node ES modules already operate under strict semantics.

