# 37. Show why the browser cannot do this

Ask:

> “Can browser JavaScript safely access the server's filesystem?”

No.

But Node:

```js
fs.readFileSync(...)
```

can.

So the environments have different powers.

Create this conceptual table:

| Capability | Browser | Node |
|---|---:|---:|
| DOM | ✅ | ❌ |
| `window` | ✅ | ❌ |
| `document` | ✅ | ❌ |
| Read arbitrary files | ❌ | ✅ |
| HTTP server | ❌ | ✅ |
| Database access | via server/API | ✅ |
| `process` | ❌ | ✅ |
| `localStorage` | ✅ | ❌ |
| Network sockets | Restricted | ✅ |
| `fetch` | ✅ | ✅ modern Node |
| JavaScript | ✅ | ✅ |

Important:

> `fetch` existing in Node does **not** make Node a browser.

