# 42. Suggested 3-hour classroom flow

If you have around 3 hours, I'd structure it like this:

| Time | Topic | Demo |
|---|---|---|
| 0–10 min | Where does JS run? | Browser vs Node |
| 10–25 | JS vs runtime/environment | `window`, `document`, `process` |
| 25–40 | What is Node? | `node index.js` |
| 40–55 | Node APIs | `process`, `fs`, `path` |
| 55–70 | Modules | browser modules |
| 70–90 | CommonJS | `require`, `module.exports` |
| 90–105 | ES Modules in Node | `import/export` |
| 105–120 | npm | `npm init`, install package |
| 120–135 | HTTP fundamentals | request/response |
| 135–160 | Node HTTP server | `http.createServer()` |
| 160–180 | Serve HTML | `fs + http` |
| 180–205 | API | `/api/message` |
| 205–225 | Browser ↔ Node | `fetch()` |
| 225–250 | Mini-project | Student API |
| 250–270 | Industry practices | structure/env/errors |

